+++ b/AUTO_RESUME_DOWNLOAD_V7_0_87.md	2026-10-24 06:29:03.247350187 +0000
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+# AutoVideo 7.0.87: automatic resume after an interrupted Flow image download
+
+## What was wrong
+
+Job `20261024-101502-7-small-daily-habits-tha-debf` stopped with "automatic pause is disabled" after
+`shot_006` failed. The log showed `FlowBrowserClosedError: Image download target closed` on every
+download attempt, and each time the browser target closed about two seconds after the download event.
+Auto-resume never started, for three reasons:
+
+1. **The retry decision looked at the wrong error.** The image recovery wraps the browser-closed error in
+   `FlowRequestPending("Image recovery checkpoint retained: ...")`. The strict frame failure treated every
+   `FlowRequestPending` as final, so the job failed immediately.
+2. **A blocked saved request was never retried.** Even after a retry, `run_job` reconciled the saved
+   request, found the download still interrupted, and stopped with "Saved request unresolved". That stop was
+   not recorded as recoverable, so the Studio supervisor never picked the job up.
+3. **Manual runs did not record the wait.** `cli.py v3 resume` and the automation helpers called `run_job`
+   directly. Only the Studio job thread recorded the stop, so a manual run could never hand over to the
+   supervisor.
+
+## What changed
+
+- **Download-only retry.** A saved image whose download was interrupted (browser closed, network, or service
+  busy) is retried automatically. The retry only reopens the exact saved project, waits, and downloads. It
+  never uploads, fills, or sends a prompt, and never spends credits.
+- **Blocked but recoverable requests wait.** When the only blocker is such a download interruption, the job
+  records an automatic-resume wait and returns `paused`. Studio's supervisor retries it with backoff
+  (2, 5, 10, 20, 30, 60 minutes, up to 8 automatic resumes), while Studio is running and the computer is awake.
+- **Unchanged protections.** A submitted request whose download is unknown still stops for a manual decision.
+  Sign-in, quota, approval and missing-file stops are never retried. A pending request with no recoverable
+  cause still stops with no wait.
+- **Every caller records the outcome.** The CLI create and resume commands and the automation helpers call
+  the same recording step as the Studio job thread.
+- **Diagnostic.** The "Image download target closed" message now includes the download URL scheme
+  (`https`, `blob`, `data`, `other`, or `unavailable`). It never shows the URL. The scheme shows why the HTTPS
+  fallback could not run. Please send it with the next runtime log.
+
+## Still open
+
+- The download target closes right after the download event. The cause is not confirmed. The scheme
+  diagnostic will show whether the browser hands over a `blob:` URL, which the HTTPS fallback cannot read.
+- The storyboard scan also treats temporary `*.probe-*.jpg` download files as frames. A probe that matches a
+  reference image is quarantined, which is correct. The behaviour is noisy but not the cause of this failure.
+- Video recovery has the same wrapper pattern but is not covered by this automatic retry. The change is limited
+  to image downloads.
+
+## For the failed job (20261024-101502-7-small-daily-habits-tha-debf)
+
+Nothing needs to change in the job. Its saved request is download-only. Either run
+`python3 cli.py v3 resume 20261024-101502-7-small-daily-habits-tha-debf` once Chrome is open and Flow is signed in,
+or keep Studio open and let the automatic resume run.
+
+## Upgrade
+
+From a 7.0.86 installation, run `python3 ../AutoVideoAI-v7.0.87/tools/update_v786_to_v787.py .` for a dry run,
+then add `--apply`. Stop the dashboard first. Chunk size for Gemini TTS remains 2400 characters by default.
